# WASM Plugin Capability Monitor (hard)

Whenever this agent **creates a new git branch** for WorldForge plan or feature work, also run the weekly host-capability check below.

**Authoritative tracker:** [`docs/development/wasm_plugin_capability_monitor.md`](docs/development/wasm_plugin_capability_monitor.md)  
(Stamp redirect: `docs/photocraft/abi_capability_check.md`)

## When

Trigger on any of:

1. `git checkout -b …` / `git switch -c …` (new branch)
2. Plan **Branch first** step (new plan/feature tip)
3. Human asks to start a new plan or feature branch

Skip only when the human explicitly says to skip the host check for this branch.

## Cadence

1. Read **Last checked:** in the monitor markdown.
2. If **fewer than 7 days** have passed → note “ABI check current” and continue (unless the human asks for a refresh).
3. If **7+ days**, missing stamp, or unreadable file → run a fresh check **in the same turn** as the branch create (before heavy implementation).

## What to check

Follow the **Official sources** and **Weekly inspection procedure** sections in the monitor file. At minimum:

| Host | Doc |
|------|-----|
| PhotoCraft | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/storytold/photocraft/main/docs/plugins.md |
| VectorCraft | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/storytold/vectorcraft/main/docs/plugins.md |
| EffectCraft (separate ABI — do not mix) | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/storytold/effectcraft/main/docs/plugins.md |

Also skim PhotoCraft #662 (v2 design), #12458 (WorldForge requests), and recent plugin-related PRs when time allows.

## Record findings in tables

Update the monitor markdown in the **same turn**:

1. Bump **Last checked** (ISO date + timezone).
2. Add/update rows in the **Capability table** (`Released` / `In development` / `Proposed` / `Requested` / `Deprecated`).
3. Add a **Weekly review log** entry (and breaking-change row if needed).
4. Call out **WorldForge opportunity** for any new **Released** feature.

## Hard limits

1. **Never implement Proposed** features in `worldforge-photocraft`.
2. **Never invent** host imports, panels, or ABI exports absent from Released upstream docs.
3. **Never assume** EffectCraft or VectorCraft APIs work inside PhotoCraft.
4. If something useful is **Released**, tell the human and note a follow-up todo/plan — do not silently rewrite the adapter mid-unrelated feature unless ordered.

